# AutoSocial AI

AutoSocial AI is a lightweight, autonomous, AI-powered Instagram posting system designed for a single owner. 
It operates as a modular monolith that researches, generates, schedules, and publishes content without human intervention.

## Architecture & Workflow

The architecture is built for simplicity, resilience, and strict separation of concerns. `instagrapi` is treated purely as an external dependency hidden behind the `PublisherInterface`. Business logic components never directly invoke the unofficial Instagram API.

**Autonomous Workflow:**
Research &rarr; Trend Detection &rarr; Memory Check &rarr; Generate Content &rarr; Generate Caption &rarr; Generate Hashtags &rarr; Recommend Music &rarr; Select Template &rarr; Render Graphic &rarr; Queue &rarr; Publish (via InstagrapiPublisher) &rarr; Collect Analytics &rarr; Store Memory &rarr; Optimize Future Posts

## Module Structure

```
autosocial/
├── src/autosocial/
│   ├── analytics/        # Collects and stores post performance metrics
│   ├── brain/            # Main orchestrator / state machine for the workflow
│   ├── cleanup/          # Garbage collection for temporary rendered files/caches
│   ├── content/          # Generators for Content, Captions, Hashtags, and Music
│   ├── core/             # Configuration, Interfaces (e.g., PublisherInterface), Exceptions
│   ├── dashboard/        # Lightweight UI for monitoring queue, calendar, and analytics
│   ├── memory/           # Memory Engine to track past content and avoid duplicates
│   ├── models/           # Shared Pydantic data models
│   ├── publishers/       # Implementations of PublisherInterface (InstagrapiPublisher)
│   ├── queue/            # Queue manager (Pending, Rendering, Publishing, Published, Failed, Retry)
│   ├── renderers/        # HTML/CSS/Playwright engine for generating graphics from templates
│   ├── research/         # Information gathering from RSS, blogs, and defined sources
│   ├── scheduler/        # Task scheduling and posting window logic
│   ├── trends/           # Trend detection and ranking
│   └── utils/            # Logging and shared utilities
```

## Dependency Graph

```mermaid
graph TD
    Scheduler --> Brain
    Brain --> ResearchEngine
    Brain --> TrendDetection
    Brain --> MemoryEngine
    Brain --> ContentGenerator
    ContentGenerator --> CaptionGenerator
    ContentGenerator --> HashtagGenerator
    ContentGenerator --> MusicRecommendation
    Brain --> HTMLRenderer
    HTMLRenderer --> QueueManager
    QueueManager --> InstagrapiPublisher
    InstagrapiPublisher --> Instagrapi[instagrapi (Third Party)]
    InstagrapiPublisher --> AnalyticsCollector
    AnalyticsCollector --> MemoryEngine
    QueueManager --> CleanupService
```

## Implementation Plan for Next Phase (Phase 3)

1. **Memory & Content Generation**: Implement the `MemoryEngine` (SQLite/JSON store) and `ContentGenerator` utilizing a chosen LLM to create unique concepts.
2. **HTML Renderer Core**: Build the baseline Playwright automation in `renderers` that takes an HTML/CSS template and outputs a `.png` or `.mp4`.
3. **Queue Manager & Scheduler Skeleton**: Wire up a lightweight SQLite or Redis-based queue to transition posts between states (Pending &rarr; Rendering &rarr; Publishing &rarr; Published).
4. **Brain Orchestrator**: Connect the pipeline from Research to the Queue.

*Note: Enterprise features like RBAC, Multi-tenancy, and complex microservices have been strictly removed.*
